    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17467" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fā^brātĕrĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in Latium</i>, <i>situated on the Via Latina</i>, now <i>S.
				Giovanni in Carico</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				9, 24, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1, 15, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 3,
				224</span></i>.—<i>Its inhabitants</i> are
			called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fabrāterni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i><span class="en">Cic. Clu.
				68, 192</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 8, 19, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				9, § 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
				101 sq.</span></i></div>
